IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `au-part5-interpretation`

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1901 (Australia): PART 5, the rules of reading (pass 2).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Pass 1 left these sections inert as "interpretive canons" or as addressing officials. They are
-- rules, and each is encoded here as a function over a small typed representation of what the rule operates on: the kind of
-- reference, the kind of person, the candidate readings. A judgment the Act leaves to the interpreter (which reading best
-- achieves the purpose; whether two wordings express the same idea) is a plain BOOLEAN input and is never guessed.
-- Where the rule is a gate ("In any Act", "Where an Act ...") a case outside the gate returns NOTHING, the explicit
-- "not covered" value, and the tests assert it. A rule with one answer is still a rule.
-- The pass-1 rules of this Part are in au-part5-interpretation.l4 (ss 13, 15AB(1), 15B(1)(2)(4)(a), 15C, 18B(1)-(3), 25A-25D).

§ `Part 5: General interpretation rules (the rules of reading)`

§§ `Section 12: every section a substantive enactment`

-- src:310 | 12 Every section a substantive enactment
-- src:311 | Every section of an Act shall have effect as a substantive enactment without introductory words.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 12 (src:310-311)
GIVEN `it is a section of an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`has effect as a substantive enactment without introductory words` `it is a section of an Act` MEANS
    IF `it is a section of an Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 15A: Acts are read subject to the Constitution`

DECLARE `How section 15A treats an enactment` IS ONE OF
    `read and construed subject to the Constitution, and valid`
    `valid to the extent to which it is not in excess of the legislative power of the Commonwealth`

-- src:327 | 15A Construction of Acts to be subject to Constitution
-- src:328 | Every Act shall be read and construed subject to the Constitution, and so as not to exceed the legislative power of the Commonwealth, to the intent that where any enactment thereof would, but for this section, have been construed as being in excess of that power, it shall nevertheless be a valid enactment to the extent to which it is not in excess of that power.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 15A (src:327-328)
GIVEN `it is an enactment of an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `but for this section it would have been construed as being in excess of the legislative power of the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `How section 15A treats an enactment`
`section 15A treats the enactment` `it is an enactment of an Act` `but for this section it would have been construed as being in excess of the legislative power of the Commonwealth` MEANS
    IF NOT `it is an enactment of an Act`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `but for this section it would have been construed as being in excess of the legislative power of the Commonwealth`
         THEN JUST `valid to the extent to which it is not in excess of the legislative power of the Commonwealth`
         ELSE JUST `read and construed subject to the Constitution, and valid`

§§ `Section 15AA: the interpretation that best achieves the purpose or object`

DECLARE `A candidate interpretation` HAS
    `its wording`                                                           IS A STRING
    `it would best achieve the purpose or object of the Act`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `that purpose or object is expressly stated in the Act`                 IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:329 | 15AA Interpretation best achieving Act’s purpose or object
-- src:330 | In interpreting a provision of an Act, the interpretation that would best achieve the purpose or object of the Act (whether or not that purpose or object is expressly stated in the Act) is to be preferred to each other interpretation.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 15AA (src:329-330)
GIVEN candidates IS A LIST OF `A candidate interpretation`
GIVETH A MAYBE `A candidate interpretation`
`the interpretation to be preferred` candidates MEANS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN c YIELD c's `it would best achieve the purpose or object of the Act`) candidates
    WHEN best FOLLOWED BY EMPTY THEN JUST best
    OTHERWISE NOTHING


§§ `Section 15AB(2) and (3): extrinsic material`

DECLARE `Material not forming part of the Act` IS ONE OF
    `matters set out in the document containing the text of the Act as printed by the Government Printer`
    `a relevant report of a Royal Commission, Law Reform Commission, committee of inquiry or other similar body`
    `a relevant report of a committee of the Parliament or of either House`
    `a treaty or other international agreement that is referred to in the Act`
    `an explanatory memorandum relating to the Bill, or any other relevant document, laid before or furnished to the members of either House by a Minister`
    `the Minister's second reading speech on the Bill containing the provision`
    `a document declared by the Act to be a relevant document for the purposes of section 15AB`
    `relevant material in the Journals of the Senate, the Votes and Proceedings of the House of Representatives or an official record of debates`
    `other material`

-- 15AB(2) says "includes": the list does not limit subsection (1). A report, memorandum or paper listed in (b), (c) or (e) is
-- listed only if it was laid or made before the time when the provision was enacted.
-- src:337 | (2) Without limiting the generality of subsection (1), the material that may be considered in accordance with that subsection in the interpretation of a provision of an Act includes:
-- src:338 | (a) all matters not forming part of the Act that are set out in the document containing the text of the Act as printed by the Government Printer;
-- src:339 | (b) any relevant report of a Royal Commission, Law Reform Commission, committee of inquiry or other similar body that was laid before either House of the Parliament before the time when the provision was enacted;
-- src:340 | (c) any relevant report of a committee of the Parliament or of either House of the Parliament that was made to the Parliament or that House of the Parliament before the time when the provision was enacted;
-- src:341 | (d) any treaty or other international agreement that is referred to in the Act;
-- src:342 | (e) any explanatory memorandum relating to the Bill containing the provision, or any other relevant document, that was laid before, or furnished to the members of, either House of the Parliament by a Minister before the time when the provision was enacted;
-- src:343 | (f) the speech made to a House of the Parliament by a Minister on the occasion of the moving by that Minister of a motion that the Bill containing the provision be read a second time in that House;
-- src:344 | (g) any document (whether or not a document to which a preceding paragraph applies) that is declared by the Act to be a relevant document for the purposes of this section; and
-- src:345 | (h) any relevant material in the Journals of the Senate, in the Votes and Proceedings of the House of Representatives or in any official record of debates in the Parliament or either House of the Parliament.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 15AB(2) (src:337-345)
GIVEN material IS A `Material not forming part of the Act`
      `it was laid before, made to or furnished to the Parliament or a House before the time when the provision was enacted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 15AB(2) lists` material `it was laid before, made to or furnished to the Parliament or a House before the time when the provision was enacted` MEANS
    CONSIDER material
    WHEN `matters set out in the document containing the text of the Act as printed by the Government Printer` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a relevant report of a Royal Commission, Law Reform Commission, committee of inquiry or other similar body` THEN `it was laid before, made to or furnished to the Parliament or a House before the time when the provision was enacted`
    WHEN `a relevant report of a committee of the Parliament or of either House` THEN `it was laid before, made to or furnished to the Parliament or a House before the time when the provision was enacted`
    WHEN `a treaty or other international agreement that is referred to in the Act` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an explanatory memorandum relating to the Bill, or any other relevant document, laid before or furnished to the members of either House by a Minister` THEN `it was laid before, made to or furnished to the Parliament or a House before the time when the provision was enacted`
    WHEN `the Minister's second reading speech on the Bill containing the provision` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a document declared by the Act to be a relevant document for the purposes of section 15AB` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `relevant material in the Journals of the Senate, the Votes and Proceedings of the House of Representatives or an official record of debates` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `other material` THEN FALSE

-- Listing is not enough: the material may be considered "in accordance with" subsection (1), whose conditions are the rule
-- `consideration may be given to the material` of au-part5-interpretation.l4.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 15AB(2) (src:337-345)
GIVEN material IS A `Material not forming part of the Act`
      `it was laid before, made to or furnished to the Parliament or a House before the time when the provision was enacted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `material not forming part of the Act is capable of assisting in the ascertainment of the meaning of the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is to confirm that the meaning is the ordinary meaning conveyed by the text, taking account of its context in the Act and the purpose or object underlying the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is ambiguous or obscure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that ordinary meaning leads to a result that is manifestly absurd or is unreasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`listed material may be considered under section 15AB(1)` material `it was laid before, made to or furnished to the Parliament or a House before the time when the provision was enacted` `material not forming part of the Act is capable of assisting in the ascertainment of the meaning of the provision` `the use is to confirm that the meaning is the ordinary meaning conveyed by the text, taking account of its context in the Act and the purpose or object underlying the Act` `the provision is ambiguous or obscure` `that ordinary meaning leads to a result that is manifestly absurd or is unreasonable` MEANS
        `section 15AB(2) lists` material `it was laid before, made to or furnished to the Parliament or a House before the time when the provision was enacted`
    AND `consideration may be given to the material` `material not forming part of the Act is capable of assisting in the ascertainment of the meaning of the provision` `the use is to confirm that the meaning is the ordinary meaning conveyed by the text, taking account of its context in the Act and the purpose or object underlying the Act` `the provision is ambiguous or obscure` `that ordinary meaning leads to a result that is manifestly absurd or is unreasonable`

DECLARE `Matter to which regard must be had under section 15AB(3)` IS ONE OF
    `the desirability of persons being able to rely on the ordinary meaning conveyed by the text of the provision taking into account its context in the Act and the purpose or object underlying the Act`
    `the need to avoid prolonging legal or other proceedings without compensating advantage`
    `any other relevant matter`
    `a matter that is not relevant`

-- In deciding whether to consider material, or what weight to give it, regard "shall be had, in addition to any other relevant
-- matters" to the two listed matters. How much weight each carries is the interpreter's judgment and is not encoded.
-- src:346 | (3) In determining whether consideration should be given to any material in accordance with subsection (1), or in considering the weight to be given to any such material, regard shall be had, in addition to any other relevant matters, to:
-- src:347 | (a) the desirability of persons being able to rely on the ordinary meaning conveyed by the text of the provision taking into account its context in the Act and the purpose or object underlying the Act; and
-- src:348 | (b) the need to avoid prolonging legal or other proceedings without compensating advantage.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 15AB(3) (src:346-348)
GIVEN matter IS A `Matter to which regard must be had under section 15AB(3)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regard must be had to` matter MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `the desirability of persons being able to rely on the ordinary meaning conveyed by the text of the provision taking into account its context in the Act and the purpose or object underlying the Act` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the need to avoid prolonging legal or other proceedings without compensating advantage` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `any other relevant matter` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a matter that is not relevant` THEN FALSE

§§ `Section 15AC: changes to style not to affect meaning`

-- src:349 | 15AC Changes to style not to affect meaning
-- src:350 | Where:
-- src:351 | (a) an Act has expressed an idea in a particular form of words; and
-- src:352 | (b) a later Act appears to have expressed the same idea in a different form of words for the purpose of using a clearer style;
-- src:353 | the ideas shall not be taken to be different merely because different forms of words were used.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 15AC (src:349-353)
GIVEN `an Act has expressed an idea in a particular form of words` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a later Act appears to have expressed the same idea in a different form of words for the purpose of using a clearer style` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the ideas are taken to be different merely because different forms of words were used` `an Act has expressed an idea in a particular form of words` `a later Act appears to have expressed the same idea in a different form of words for the purpose of using a clearer style` MEANS
    IF `an Act has expressed an idea in a particular form of words` AND `a later Act appears to have expressed the same idea in a different form of words for the purpose of using a clearer style`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 15AD: examples`

-- src:354 | 15AD Examples
-- src:355 | If an Act includes an example of the operation of a provision:
-- src:356 | (a) the example is not exhaustive; and
-- src:357 | (b) the example may extend the operation of the provision.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 15AD (src:354-357)
GIVEN `an Act includes an example of the operation of a provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the example is exhaustive` `an Act includes an example of the operation of a provision` MEANS
    IF `an Act includes an example of the operation of a provision` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 15AD(b) (src:357)
GIVEN `an Act includes an example of the operation of a provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the example may extend the operation of the provision` `an Act includes an example of the operation of a provision` MEANS
    IF `an Act includes an example of the operation of a provision` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING


§§ `Section 15B(3), (3A) and (4)(b): the coastal sea of an external Territory`

-- The same shape as subsections (1), (2) and (4)(a) (au-part5-interpretation.l4), for a Territory whose coastal sea is
-- adjacent to it.
-- src:363 | (3) An Act that is in force in an external Territory is taken to have effect in, and in relation to, the coastal sea of the Territory as if that coastal sea were part of the Territory.
-- src:364 | (3A) A reference in an Act to all or any of the external Territories (whether or not one or more particular Territories are referred to) is taken to include a reference to the coastal sea of any Territory to which the reference relates.
-- src:365 | Definition
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 15B(3) and (3A) (src:363-365)
GIVEN `the Act is in force in an external Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the place is in the coastal sea of that Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an Act in force in an external Territory is taken to have effect in its coastal sea as if it were part of the Territory` `the Act is in force in an external Territory` `the place is in the coastal sea of that Territory` MEANS
    `the Act is in force in an external Territory` AND `the place is in the coastal sea of that Territory`

@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 15B(3A) (src:364-365)
GIVEN `the reference is to all or any of the external Territories, whether or not particular Territories are referred to` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sea is the coastal sea of a Territory to which the reference relates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the reference to the external Territories is taken to include the coastal sea` `the reference is to all or any of the external Territories, whether or not particular Territories are referred to` `the sea is the coastal sea of a Territory to which the reference relates` MEANS
    `the reference is to all or any of the external Territories, whether or not particular Territories are referred to` AND `the sea is the coastal sea of a Territory to which the reference relates`

-- src:371 | (b) in relation to an external Territory, means:
-- src:372 | (i) the territorial sea adjacent to the Territory; and
-- src:373 | (ii) the sea on the landward side of the territorial sea adjacent to the Territory and not within the limits of the Territory;
-- src:374 | and includes the airspace over, and the sea-bed and subsoil beneath, any such sea.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 15B(4)(b) (src:371-374)
GIVEN `it is in the territorial sea adjacent to the Territory, or in its airspace, sea-bed or subsoil` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in the sea on the landward side of the territorial sea adjacent to the Territory and not within the limits of the Territory, or in its airspace, sea-bed or subsoil` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is in the coastal sea of an external Territory` `it is in the territorial sea adjacent to the Territory, or in its airspace, sea-bed or subsoil` `it is in the sea on the landward side of the territorial sea adjacent to the Territory and not within the limits of the Territory, or in its airspace, sea-bed or subsoil` MEANS
        `it is in the territorial sea adjacent to the Territory, or in its airspace, sea-bed or subsoil`
     OR `it is in the sea on the landward side of the territorial sea adjacent to the Territory and not within the limits of the Territory, or in its airspace, sea-bed or subsoil`

§§ `Sections 16 to 17A: references to the Sovereign, the Governor-General, a State Governor, judges, magistrates and the Government Printer`

DECLARE `A reference to the Sovereign or the Crown` IS ONE OF
    `a reference to the Sovereign reigning at the time of the passing of the Act`
    `a reference to the Crown`
    `a reference to anyone else`

DECLARE `Whom a reference is construed as meaning` IS ONE OF
    `the Sovereign for the time being`

-- src:380 | 16 References to the Sovereign
-- src:381 | In any Act references to the Sovereign reigning at the time of the passing of such Act, or to the Crown, shall be construed as references to the Sovereign for the time being.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 16 (src:380-381)
GIVEN reference IS A `A reference to the Sovereign or the Crown`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Whom a reference is construed as meaning`
`a reference in an Act is construed as a reference to` reference MEANS
    CONSIDER reference
    WHEN `a reference to the Sovereign reigning at the time of the passing of the Act` THEN JUST `the Sovereign for the time being`
    WHEN `a reference to the Crown` THEN JUST `the Sovereign for the time being`
    WHEN `a reference to anyone else` THEN NOTHING

DECLARE `Who may be meant by a reference to the Governor-General` IS ONE OF
    `the Governor-General`
    `the person for the time being administering the Government of the Commonwealth`
    `a person to whom the Governor-General or the administrator has for the time being assigned a power or function as deputy`
    `anyone else`

-- src:382 | 16A References to the Governor-General
-- src:383 | Where, in an Act, the Governor-General is referred to, the reference shall be deemed to include:
-- src:384 | (a) the person for the time being administering the Government of the Commonwealth; or
-- src:385 | (b) where the reference occurs in or in relation to a provision conferring on the Governor-General a power or function which the Governor-General or the person administering the Government of the Commonwealth has for the time being assigned to a person as his or her deputy, that last-mentioned person in his or her capacity as deputy;
-- src:386 | and shall be read as referring to the Governor-General, or a person so deemed to be included in the reference, acting with the advice of the Executive Council.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 16A (src:382-386)
GIVEN person IS A `Who may be meant by a reference to the Governor-General`
      `the reference occurs in or in relation to a provision conferring a power or function that has been assigned to that person as deputy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a reference to the Governor-General is deemed to include` person `the reference occurs in or in relation to a provision conferring a power or function that has been assigned to that person as deputy` MEANS
    CONSIDER person
    WHEN `the Governor-General` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the person for the time being administering the Government of the Commonwealth` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a person to whom the Governor-General or the administrator has for the time being assigned a power or function as deputy` THEN `the reference occurs in or in relation to a provision conferring a power or function that has been assigned to that person as deputy`
    WHEN `anyone else` THEN FALSE

-- "and shall be read as referring to the Governor-General, or a person so deemed to be included in the reference, acting with
-- the advice of the Executive Council".
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 16A (src:385-386)
GIVEN person IS A `Who may be meant by a reference to the Governor-General`
      `the reference occurs in or in relation to a provision conferring a power or function that has been assigned to that person as deputy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the reference is read as acting with the advice of the Executive Council` person `the reference occurs in or in relation to a provision conferring a power or function that has been assigned to that person as deputy` MEANS
    `a reference to the Governor-General is deemed to include` person `the reference occurs in or in relation to a provision conferring a power or function that has been assigned to that person as deputy`

DECLARE `Who may be meant by a reference to the Governor of a State` IS ONE OF
    `the Governor for the time being of the State`
    `another person who is for the time being the chief executive officer or administrator of the government of the State`
    `anyone else`

-- src:387 | 16B References to the Governor of a State
-- src:388 | Where, in an Act, the Governor of a State is referred to, the reference shall be deemed to include the Governor for the time being of the State or any other person who is, for the time being, the chief executive officer or administrator of the government of the State.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 16B (src:387-388)
GIVEN person IS A `Who may be meant by a reference to the Governor of a State`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a reference to the Governor of a State is deemed to include` person MEANS
    CONSIDER person
    WHEN `the Governor for the time being of the State` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `another person who is for the time being the chief executive officer or administrator of the government of the State` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `anyone else` THEN FALSE

DECLARE `Kind of judge` IS ONE OF
    `a Judge or acting Judge of the Local Court of New South Wales`
    `a Judge or acting Judge of the Local Court of the Northern Territory`
    `any other judge`

-- Section 16BA only takes the two Local Courts out. Whether any other judge is a "judge" is the ordinary meaning of the word,
-- which the section does not decide: NOTHING.
-- src:389 | 16BA References to judge
-- src:390 | In any Act, a reference (whether general or otherwise) to a judge does not include a reference to a Judge, or an acting Judge, of the Local Court of New South Wales or of the Local Court of the Northern Territory.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 16BA (src:389-390)
GIVEN judge IS A `Kind of judge`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a reference to a judge includes` judge MEANS
    CONSIDER judge
    WHEN `a Judge or acting Judge of the Local Court of New South Wales` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `a Judge or acting Judge of the Local Court of the Northern Territory` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `any other judge` THEN NOTHING

DECLARE `Kind of magistrate` IS ONE OF
    `a Stipendiary Magistrate`
    `a Chief Magistrate`
    `a Police Magistrate`
    `a Resident Magistrate`
    `a Special Magistrate`
    `any other Magistrate`
    `a Judge or acting Judge of the Local Court of New South Wales`
    `a Judge or acting Judge of the Local Court of the Northern Territory`

-- Section 16C(1): a reference to a Stipendiary Magistrate includes any Magistrate whose office carries an annual salary; (3): and
-- includes a Judge or acting Judge of either Local Court.
-- src:391 | 16C References to Stipendiary Magistrate and Magistrate
-- src:392 | (1) Where, in an Act, reference is made to a Stipendiary Magistrate, the reference shall be read as including a reference to any Magistrate in respect of whose office an annual salary is payable.
-- src:396 | (3) In any Act, a reference to a Stipendiary Magistrate or Magistrate includes a reference to a Judge, or an acting Judge, of the Local Court of New South Wales or of the Local Court of the Northern Territory.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 16C(1) and (3) (src:391-396)
GIVEN magistrate IS A `Kind of magistrate`
      `an annual salary is payable in respect of the office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a reference to a Stipendiary Magistrate includes` magistrate `an annual salary is payable in respect of the office` MEANS
    CONSIDER magistrate
    WHEN `a Judge or acting Judge of the Local Court of New South Wales` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a Judge or acting Judge of the Local Court of the Northern Territory` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a Stipendiary Magistrate` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE `an annual salary is payable in respect of the office`

-- Section 16C(2): in an Act passed after the date of commencement of s 16C, a reference to a Magistrate is a reference to a Chief,
-- Police, Stipendiary, Resident or Special Magistrate, or any other Magistrate whose office carries an annual salary; (3) adds the
-- Local Court Judges to a reference to a Magistrate in any Act. The text does not give the date of commencement of s 16C (fork F18):
-- the Act's date is an input, and for an earlier Act subsection (2) says nothing about the named titles.
-- src:393 | (2) Where, in an Act passed after the date of commencement of this section, reference is made to a Magistrate, the reference shall be read as a reference to:
-- src:394 | (a) a Chief, Police, Stipendiary, Resident or Special Magistrate; or
-- src:395 | (b) any other Magistrate in respect of whose office an annual salary is payable.
-- src:396 | (3) In any Act, a reference to a Stipendiary Magistrate or Magistrate includes a reference to a Judge, or an acting Judge, of the Local Court of New South Wales or of the Local Court of the Northern Territory.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 16C(2) and (3) (src:393-396)
GIVEN magistrate IS A `Kind of magistrate`
      `an annual salary is payable in respect of the office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act was passed after the date of commencement of section 16C` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a reference to a Magistrate includes` magistrate `an annual salary is payable in respect of the office` `the Act was passed after the date of commencement of section 16C` MEANS
    CONSIDER magistrate
    WHEN `a Judge or acting Judge of the Local Court of New South Wales` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a Judge or acting Judge of the Local Court of the Northern Territory` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the Act was passed after the date of commencement of section 16C`
        THEN JUST (   magistrate EQUALS `a Chief Magistrate`
                   OR magistrate EQUALS `a Police Magistrate`
                   OR magistrate EQUALS `a Stipendiary Magistrate`
                   OR magistrate EQUALS `a Resident Magistrate`
                   OR magistrate EQUALS `a Special Magistrate`
                   OR `an annual salary is payable in respect of the office`)
        ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Words printed on a paper or document` IS ONE OF
    `Government Printer of the Commonwealth`
    `Government Printer of the Commonwealth of Australia`
    `Commonwealth Government Printer`
    `Government Printer of Australia`
    `other words`

-- src:397 | 17A Paper or document purporting to be printed by Government Printer
-- src:398 | For the purposes of an Act in which reference is made to a paper or document purporting to be printed by the Government Printer, the words “Government Printer of the Commonwealth”, “Government Printer of the Commonwealth of Australia”, “Commonwealth Government Printer” or “Government Printer of Australia” appearing on a paper or document shall be deemed to refer to the Government Printer.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 17A (src:397-398)
GIVEN words IS A `Words printed on a paper or document`
      `an Act refers to a paper or document purporting to be printed by the Government Printer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the words are deemed to refer to the Government Printer` words `an Act refers to a paper or document purporting to be printed by the Government Printer` MEANS
    IF NOT `an Act refers to a paper or document purporting to be printed by the Government Printer`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER words
         WHEN `other words` THEN NOTHING
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `Section 18A: parts of speech and grammatical forms`

DECLARE `Form of a word or phrase` IS ONE OF
    `the word or phrase as it is given its particular meaning`
    `another part of speech of that word or phrase`
    `another grammatical form of that word or phrase`
    `a different word or phrase`

-- src:399 | 18A Parts of speech and grammatical forms
-- src:400 | In any Act where a word or phrase is given a particular meaning, other parts of speech and grammatical forms of that word or phrase have corresponding meanings.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 18A (src:399-400)
GIVEN form IS A `Form of a word or phrase`
      `the Act gives the word or phrase a particular meaning` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`has a corresponding meaning` form `the Act gives the word or phrase a particular meaning` MEANS
    IF NOT `the Act gives the word or phrase a particular meaning`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER form
         WHEN `another part of speech of that word or phrase` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `another grammatical form of that word or phrase` THEN JUST TRUE
         OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `Section 18B(4) to (6): titles of Deputy Chairs`

DECLARE `Deputy chair title` IS ONE OF `Deputy Chair`, `Deputy Chairperson`, `Deputy Chairman`, `Deputy Chairwoman`

-- src:414 | (4) For the purposes of this section, each of the following is a deputy chair title:
-- src:415 | (a) Deputy Chair;
-- src:416 | (b) Deputy Chairperson;
-- src:417 | (c) Deputy Chairman;
-- src:418 | (d) Deputy Chairwoman.
-- src:419 | (5) A person occupying an office that is established by an Act and that has a deputy chair title may choose to be referred to by:
-- src:420 | (a) that deputy chair title; or
-- src:421 | (b) another deputy chair title; or
-- src:422 | (c) any other similar title.
-- src:423 | (6) If a person occupying an office that is established by an Act and that has a deputy chair title does not choose to be referred to by a title mentioned in subsection (5), the person may be referred to by the deputy chair title that someone addressing the person considers appropriate.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 18B(4) to (6) (src:414-423)
GIVEN `the person occupies an office established by an Act that has a deputy chair title` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has chosen to be referred to by this deputy chair title, another deputy chair title or a similar title` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has not chosen a title` IS A BOOLEAN
      `someone addressing the person considers this deputy chair title appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person may be referred to by this deputy chair title` `the person occupies an office established by an Act that has a deputy chair title` `the person has chosen to be referred to by this deputy chair title, another deputy chair title or a similar title` `the person has not chosen a title` `someone addressing the person considers this deputy chair title appropriate` MEANS
        `the person occupies an office established by an Act that has a deputy chair title`
    AND (   `the person has chosen to be referred to by this deputy chair title, another deputy chair title or a similar title`
         OR (   `the person has not chosen a title`
             AND `someone addressing the person considers this deputy chair title appropriate`))


§§ `Sections 20, 21 and 23: holders of offices, the Commonwealth's offices and localities, gender and number`

DECLARE `Relation of a person to an office, appointment or position` IS ONE OF
    `holds or occupies it for the time being`
    `performs its duties for the time being`
    `neither holds nor occupies it nor performs its duties`

-- src:576 | 20 References to holders of appointments, offices and positions in Acts and Commonwealth agreements
-- src:577 | In a provision of an Act, or of an agreement entered into by or on behalf of the Commonwealth, a reference in general terms to the holder or occupier of an office, appointment or position includes all persons who for the time being:
-- src:578 | (a) hold or occupy the office, appointment or position; or
-- src:579 | (b) perform the duties of the office, appointment or position.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 20 (src:576-579)
GIVEN relation IS A `Relation of a person to an office, appointment or position`
      `the reference is in a provision of an Act, or of an agreement entered into by or on behalf of the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reference to the holder or occupier is in general terms` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a reference to the holder or occupier includes the person` relation `the reference is in a provision of an Act, or of an agreement entered into by or on behalf of the Commonwealth` `the reference to the holder or occupier is in general terms` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the reference is in a provision of an Act, or of an agreement entered into by or on behalf of the Commonwealth` AND `the reference to the holder or occupier is in general terms`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (relation EQUALS `holds or occupies it for the time being` OR relation EQUALS `performs its duties for the time being`)

DECLARE `Thing referred to in an Act` IS ONE OF
    `an officer`
    `an office`
    `a locality`
    `a jurisdiction`
    `another matter or thing`

DECLARE `What a reference to it is construed as` IS ONE OF
    `a reference to such an officer or office in and for the Commonwealth`
    `a reference to such localities, jurisdictions and other matters and things in and of the Commonwealth`

-- src:580 | 21 Office etc. means office etc. of the Commonwealth
-- src:581 | (1) In any Act:
-- src:582 | (a) references to any officer or office shall be construed as references to such officer or office in and for the Commonwealth; and
-- src:583 | (b) references to localities jurisdictions and other matters and things shall be construed as references to such localities jurisdictions and other matters and things in and of the Commonwealth.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 21(1) (src:580-583)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing referred to in an Act`
GIVETH A `What a reference to it is construed as`
`a reference in an Act to it is construed as` thing MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `an officer` THEN `a reference to such an officer or office in and for the Commonwealth`
    WHEN `an office` THEN `a reference to such an officer or office in and for the Commonwealth`
    WHEN `a locality` THEN `a reference to such localities, jurisdictions and other matters and things in and of the Commonwealth`
    WHEN `a jurisdiction` THEN `a reference to such localities, jurisdictions and other matters and things in and of the Commonwealth`
    WHEN `another matter or thing` THEN `a reference to such localities, jurisdictions and other matters and things in and of the Commonwealth`

DECLARE `Gender imported by a word` IS ONE OF
    `masculine`
    `feminine`
    `another gender`
    `no gender`

DECLARE `Number of a word` IS ONE OF `singular`, `plural`

-- src:587 | 23 Rules as to gender and number
-- src:588 | In any Act:
-- src:589 | (a) words importing a gender include every other gender; and
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 23(a) (src:587-589)
GIVEN other IS A `Gender imported by a word`, word IS A `Gender imported by a word`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`words importing a gender include` other `when the word imports` word MEANS
    IF word EQUALS `no gender` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:588 | In any Act:
-- src:589 | (a) words importing a gender include every other gender; and
-- src:590 | (b) words in the singular number include the plural and words in the plural number include the singular.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 23(b) (src:588-590)
GIVEN other IS A `Number of a word`, word IS A `Number of a word`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`words in a number include` other `when the word is in the` word MEANS
    CONSIDER word
    WHEN `singular` THEN other EQUALS `plural` OR other EQUALS `singular`
    WHEN `plural` THEN other EQUALS `singular` OR other EQUALS `plural`
